  abstract = "The golden spiny mouse is dependent on non shivering thermogenesis
              (N.S.T.) for thermoregulation at cool ambient temperatures. Mice
              from the shores of the Dead Sea (Ein-Gedi, EG-mice) lose body heat
              when exposed to 6 degrees C. Their rate of cooling is linearly
