  author   = "Michałek, Hanna and Pintor, Annita and Fortuna, S and Gm, Bisso",
  journal  = "PubMed",
  abstract = "Brain choline acetyltransferase, acetylcholinesterase with its
              molecular forms, and muscarinic receptor sites, as well as liver
              total cholinesterases were evaluated during the first postnatal
              month in pups of a precocial (Acomys cahirinus) and altricial
              (rat) murid species. At birth the levels of brain cholinergic
              markers were higher in the Acomys than in the rat, but in
              adulthood the differences were smaller or even reversed. The
              postnatal increase up in the markers to weaning was considerably
              more pronounced in the rat. However, substantial variations in the
              patterns of development of the three cholinergic markers within
