              discrimination tests with adult males from different wadis showed
              that those from sites with greater helminth abundance were less
              likely to investigate odours from other males and were less
              aggressive when subsequently interacting with the odour donors.
              Subjects showed markedly more investigation towards the odours of
              males from distant wadis compared with those from their own or
              immediately neighbouring wadi, but were less aggressive when
              confronted with odour donors from distant wadis. Despite this,
              there was a positive relationship between the amount of
              investigation towards distant male odour and subsequent aggression
