  journal  = "Parasite",
  abstract = "Monanema joopi n. sp. is described from blood drawn from the heart
              of the murid Acomys (Acomys) spinosissimus in South Africa. It is
              characterised by a non-bulbous cephalic extremity, shared with
              only one of its five congeners, and a cylindrical tail with caudal
