              the genus, microfilariae are skin-dwelling. They are 185 to 215
              micrometres long and have no refractory granules beneath their
              sheath. A key to the species of Monanema is presented and an
              amended generic description, based on the six currently known
              species, is proposed. Species of Monanema are primarily lymphatic
              and the low intensity of infection with M. joopi n. sp. in blood
              from the heart, might suggest that not all adults settle in the
              heart cavities. One might also consider that other, more
              susceptible rodents serve as hosts for this parasite as well. To
              date, the geographic range of Monanema includes North America,
