              of experiments using a multi-choice test apparatus. The animals
              were tested every fifth day from day 1 of age until 35 days. The
              tests were carried out using both a longitudinal and a
              cross-sectional design. No differences were found between the
              experimental designs. Young A. cahirinus pups (1-10 days old)
              showed a strong preference for a familiar home cage odour. This
