  volume   =  55,
  number   =  1,
  pages    = "9--17",
  abstract = "African spiny mice (Acomys spp.) are unique precocial rodents that
              are found in Africa, the Middle East, and southern Asia. They
              exhibit several interesting life-history characteristics,
              including precocial development, communal breeding, and a suite of
              physiologic adaptations to desert life. In addition to these
              characteristics, African spiny mice are emerging as an important
              animal model for tissue regeneration research. Furthermore, their
              important phylogenetic position among murid rodents makes them an
              interesting model for evolution and development studies. Here we
