              ROS production was stronger and more persistent during
              regeneration. By depleting macrophages during injury, we
              demonstrate a functional requirement for these cells to stimulate
              regeneration. Importantly, the spatial distribution of activated
              macrophage subtypes was unique during regeneration with
              pro-inflammatory macrophages failing to infiltrate the
              regeneration blastema. Together, our results demonstrate an
              essential role for inflammatory cells to regulate a regenerative
              response.",
  month    =  may,
