              Non-model organisms may, however, give us some important insights
              into how to increase neural stem cell numbers for regenerative
              purposes and with this in mind we have characterized these cells
              in the brain of the spiny mouse, Acomys cahirinus. This unique
              mammal is highly regenerative and damaged tissue does not scar or
              fibrose. We find that there are more than three times as many stem
