  journal  = "npj Regenerative medicine",
  volume   =  6,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  1,
  abstract = "The spiny mouse (Acomys species) has emerged as an exciting
              research organism due to its remarkable ability to undergo
              scarless regeneration of skin wounds and ear punches. Excitingly,
              Acomys species demonstrate scar-free healing in a wide-range of
              tissues beyond the skin. In this perspective article, we discuss
              published findings from a variety of tissues to highlight how this
              emerging research organism could shed light on numerous clinically
              relevant human diseases. We also discuss the challenges of working
              with this emerging research organism and suggest strategies for
              future Acomys-inspired research.",
