  journal  = "Bull. Psychon. Soc.",
  volume   =  23,
  number   =  3,
  pages    = "253--255",
  abstract = "Observed 8 mated pairs of adult spiny mice with their litters from
              the day before birth through Day 10 postpartum. Parent-offspring
              interactions in the amount of time each parent spent in physical
              contact with its offspring were recorded. Parental interactions
              were also recorded by measuring the amount of time the dam and
              sire were in physical contact, their activity levels, and the
              percentage of times the dam led and followed the sire through the
              home environment. Each mated pair reared its litter inside a
              4-compartment habitat enclosure. Results indicate that (a) adult
              activity levels peaked on Day 1, (b) sires accumulated
