  journal  = "BMC Evol. Biol.",
  volume   =  19,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  69,
  abstract = "Spiny mice of the genus Acomys are distributed mainly in dry open
              habitats in Africa and the Middle East, and they are widely used
              as model taxa for various biological disciplines (e.g. ecology,
              physiology and evolutionary biology). Despite their importance,
              large distribution and abundance in local communities, the
              phylogeny and the species limits in the genus are poorly resolved,
              and this is especially true for sub-Saharan taxa. The main aims of
              this study are (1) to reconstruct phylogenetic relationships of
              Acomys based on the largest available multilocus dataset (700
              genotyped individuals from 282 localities), (2) to identify the
              main biogeographical divides in the distribution of Acomys
