              several treatments and mean arterial blood pressure was monitored
              in response to several doses of AII. As expected, both water
              deprivation and hypertonic NaCl led to robust drinking with short
              latencies. PEG was also an effective dipsogen; while quite
              variable, latencies were often shorter than are typically reported
